From 2bf79471cbf06e5eddc97b1e9c35617ab7692279 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ebg-ant <296364998+ebg-ant@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:16:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: at once, and in one piece: no hole where windows leave,
 no empty desk where tiles come

Without motion a display shows every state between the first asking of an act and the last.

No hole. Windows were sent out of view first, so the desk showed through until the one that fills the screen had grown. Now
what arrives or grows is asked first, what shrinks next, and what leaves goes last, from behind what has grown. Those who leave
are foretold by themselves, when those who stay have their frames: side by side with them they would be gone first every time,
since to leave is one call for a place and to grow is a resize.

No empty desk. Where windows become tiles they were gone before the tiles were there. Now the tiles are put up first, behind the
windows, which leave from on top of them; without motion a tile does not fade in; and the icons tiles are drawn from are
fetched when a window is docked, not when the first tile is drawn.

A net reads both off the fake's log of moves, each asking taken apart as the Accessibility layer takes it apart: no window
within neither its old frame nor its new one, no ground bare that is covered before and after. The fake can carry out what is
foretold as apps do that work side by side.
